## E1 (L4) — The algorithm on a world you control

Construct a **unit-consistent price path** P (300 days, $50 start,
σ=1.5%): what the stock was "really" worth per original share. Events:
2:1 split at day 100, 3:1 at day 220, $0.50 dividends every 21 days.
The **raw as-traded series** is P ÷ cumulative split ratio. The
**holder's true return** (dividend reinvested at the ex-day close —
the provider convention):

> r_t = (P_t/P_{t−1}) · 1/(1 − D_t/P_t) − 1 on ex-dates; else P_t/P_{t−1} − 1

