## Hints

- E1: process events NEWEST to OLDEST; each event edits only the
  past: splits `factor[:t] /= ratio`; dividends
  `factor[:t] *= (1 − D/raw[t])` (raw[t] = ex-day as-traded price —
  dividends are per CURRENT share; the ground truth must use the
  same price or the unit test fails at ~1e−2, not 1e−16).
- E2: a reverse split is a split with ratio < 1 — if your code needs
  a special case, the data model is wrong, not the event.
